# write then slurp roundtrip: write "hello tinct" to /tmp, read it back
# % is used as an intermediate expression in the second document to force
# materialization of the write side-effect before the slurp runs.
[write [dir-cap "/tmp"] "tinct-test-write-slurp.txt" "hello tinct"]
---
%
[slurp [open [dir-cap "/tmp"] "tinct-test-write-slurp.txt" "r"]]
=== out
String("hello tinct")
